lance sheet, bank statements, and business registration as income proof instead of salary slips."}},{"@type":"Question",name:"What is the difference between floating and fixed home loan rates?",acceptedAnswer:{"@type":"Answer",text:"A floating rate changes with the RBI repo rate and is currently lower; a fixed rate stays constant for a set period offering predictability. Most home loans in India are offered at floating rates linked to RLLR or EBLR."}},{"@type":"Question",name:"Are there any tax benefits on a home loan?",acceptedAnswer:{"@type":"Answer",text:"Yes. Under Section 24(b) you can deduct up to ₹2 Lakh per year on interest paid. Under Section 80C, principal repayment up to ₹1.5 Lakh is deductible. First-time buyers may also claim additional deduction under Section 80EEA."}}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList",itemListElement:[{"@type":"ListItem",position:1,name:"Home",item:"https://ekpaisa.in/"},{"@type":"ListItem",position:2,name:"Home Loan",item:"https://ekpaisa.in/home-loan"}]}]};return s.jsxs("div",{className:"min-h-screen bg-white flex flex-col font-roboto selection:bg-[#76b900] selection:text-white overflow-x-hidden",children:[s.jsx(_r,{title:"Apply for Home Loan Online - Low Interest Rates - ekPaisa",description:"Apply for home loans up to ₹5 Crore with ekPaisa. Compare top bank offers, calculate EMIs, check eligibility, and get fast processing.",canonicalUrl:"https://ekpaisa.in/home-loan",keywords:"home loan, housing loan, low interest home loan, apply home loan online, fast home loan",schemaData:pe}),s.jsx("style",{children:`
