e, institution, and your family income."},{question:"Do I need collateral for an education loan?",answer:"Loans up to ₹7.5 Lakh are typically collateral-free. For higher amounts, lenders may require property, FD, or insurance as security. Some lenders offer collateral-free loans up to ₹40 Lakh for premium institutions (IITs, IIMs, top foreign universities)."},{question:"What is a moratorium period and when does repayment start?",answer:"The moratorium period is the course duration plus 6–12 months after completion (or after getting a job, whichever is earlier). You don't need to pay EMIs during this period, though some lenders ask for simple interest during moratorium."},{question:"Are there tax benefits on education loans?",answer:"Yes — under Section 80E of the Income Tax Act, the entire interest paid on an education loan is deductible from your taxable income for up to 8 years. This benefit is available only to the borrower (not the co-applicant)."},{question:"Who can be a co-applicant on an education loan?",answer:"Parents, spouse, siblings, or in-laws can be co-applicants. A co-applicant with a stable income improves your eligibility significantly. Most lenders require at least one earning co-applicant."}],VR={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage",mainEntity:r3.map(({question:r,answer:e})=>({"@type":"Question",name:r,acceptedAnswer:{"@type":"Answer",text:e}}))},FR={"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[MR,VR]},eg=({label:r,value:e,isHighlight:t})=>s.jsxs("div",{className:`flex flex-col justify-center border rounded-lg p-2.5 sm:p-3 text-center transition-all duration-300 ${t?"bg-white border-[#76b900]/30 shadow-sm":"bg-gray-50 border-gray-200"}`,children:[s.jsx("div",{className:`text-[8px] sm:text-[9px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widest mb-1 ${t?"text-[#76b900]":"text-gray-500"}`,children:r}),s.jsx("div",{className:`text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-semibold break-words tracking-tight ${t?"text-gray-900":"text-gray-700"}`,children:e})]}),BR=()=>{co